# Terrain Search Assistant — engineering rules

- Keep business logic out of Streamlit UI modules (`ui/`); views orchestrate only.
- Type all public functions; prefer explicit `None` over fabricated zeros/coordinates.
- Cover geodesic / geometry calculations with unit tests.
- Do not hardcode absolute paths, operational coordinates, or UTM zones.
- `relative_altitude` is NOT height above terrain (DEM AGL).
- Never present drone GPS as the found object's coordinates.
- Do not claim precise coverage / footprint without a DEM backend.
- Never conclude «людей нет» or that an area is safe.
- Do not delete doubtful candidates; status history must be retained.
- Do not wire ML without a `Detector` adapter; this iteration uses `NullDetector` only.
- Do not assume GPU availability.
- Do not send video/telemetry/artifacts to external services.
- Never use `subprocess` with `shell=True`.
- Do not swallow exceptions with bare `except:` / empty handlers.
- Do not add dependencies without a concrete need in the current iteration.
- Avoid large unrelated refactors without justification.
